+6. `go/admin_lights_holdout_test.go` `TestHoldoutA209FiftyOneBoundary` —
+   the page-2 count now counts ROW-LEVEL thumbnail-alt markers:
+   `strings.Count(frag, "alt=\"Boundary lamp 01\"")` must be exactly 1 AND
+   `strings.Count(frag, "alt=\"Boundary lamp ")` — one marker per row, any
+   lamp number — must be exactly 1. Together: EXACTLY ONE row on page 2 and
+   it is lamp 01; the draft's trailing
+   Contains("Boundary lamp 01") / absence-of-"Boundary lamp 02" check is
+   kept verbatim. Justification (mechanical): the draft counted raw string
+   occurrences of `Boundary lamp`, but a contract-compliant row mentions
+   the label TWICE (the frozen per-row thumbnail alt `alt="<label>"` plus
+   the frozen label link to `/admin/lights/{id}`), so
+   `strings.Count(...) != 1` could never hold on ANY compliant fragment
+   (observed: count 2 with `Boundary lamp 01` present and `02` absent —
+   one row, two mentions). **Attempt 2's first replacement — a
+   distinct-lamp-number set check (`{"01"}`) — was REJECTED by the review
+   (finding 1, the BLOCK): a DUPLICATED lamp-01 row satisfies the set, so
+   it was weaker than the draft's exactly-one-ROW boundary, and this
+   handoff then wrongly called it "strictly stronger". The attempt-3 fix
+   above restores the row-count pin: the frozen row template carries
+   exactly one `alt="…"` per row (`web/templates/partials/admin-rows.html`
+   line 6; `thumbAlt` = label for asset-less lights), so N rows yield N
+   markers — a duplicated row (2 markers), an extra Boundary row (2
+   markers), the wrong lamp (0 `01` markers) or an empty page (0 markers)
